<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>2.1.5 Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00377</md:content-id>
    <md:title>2.1.5 Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>2bc613e1-a5c3-4553-bc33-e03f37b87d60</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><div class="os-raise-familysupport">
  <para>Access the <link url="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/b62c9150250bf52d6cc37569213ab516e0090dca">Desmos guide PDF</link> for tips on solving problems with the Desmos graphing calculator.</para>
</div>
<!-- Directions -->
<para>In 1 - 4, determine if the following points are solutions to the given system of equations.</para>
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="efc0e145-7f1a-4403-b2a0-a5a829e76fc6" data-retry-limit="2" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <!-- Question 1 -->
  <exercise data-content-id="1055a4fc-c177-493d-97d8-bf3dbeb17e02" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="(3,1)" data-solution-options="[&quot;(3,1)&quot;, &quot;(-3,4)&quot;, &quot;(8/7, 6/7)&quot;, &quot;(1, 3/4)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Determine if the point is a solution to the system of equations: \(\left\{\begin{array}{l}2x-6y=0\\3x-4y=5\end{array}\right.\)</para>
      </problem>
  </exercise>
  <solution> 
    <para>Correct! Replacing x with 3 and y with 1 in both equations makes both equations true.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response"> 
    <para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.1.2.</para>
    </div>
  <!-- Question 2 -->
  <exercise data-content-id="141cdbc2-ad03-4115-afec-487a5b05ab4c" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="(-3,4)" data-solution-options="[&quot;(3,1)&quot;, &quot;(-3,4)&quot;, &quot;(8/7, 6/7)&quot;, &quot;(1, 3/4)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Determine if the point is a solution to the system of equations: \(\left\{\begin{array}{l}x-6y=0\\3x-4y=5\end{array}\right.\)</para>
      </problem>
  </exercise>
  <solution> 
    <para>Correct! Replacing x with -3 and y with 4 in both equations makes both equations true. </para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response"> 
    <para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.1.2.</para>
    </div>
  <!-- Question 3 -->
  <exercise data-content-id="d0ec0578-6e89-47cb-adea-5d9c6dca5e00" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="(8/7, 6/7)" data-solution-options="[&quot;(3,1)&quot;, &quot;(-3,4)&quot;, &quot;(8/7, 6/7)&quot;, &quot;(1, 3/4)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Determine if the point is a solution to the system of equations: \(\left\{\begin{array}{l}x + y = 2\\y = \frac{3}{4}x\end{array}\right.\)</para>
      </problem>
  </exercise>
  <solution> 
    <para>Correct! Replacing x with \(\frac{8}{7}\) and y with \(\frac{6}{7}\) in both equations makes both equations true.
    </para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response"> 
    <para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.1.2.</para>
    </div>
  <!-- Question 4 -->
  <exercise data-content-id="983346d9-18df-447b-9cdc-a373ad6d48d3" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="(1, \(\frac{3}{4}\))" data-solution-options="[&quot;(3,1)&quot;, &quot;(-3,4)&quot;, &quot;(\\(\\frac{8}{7}\\), \\(\\frac{6}{7}\\))&quot;, &quot;(1, \\(\\frac{3}{4}\\))&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Determine if the point is a solution to the system of equations: \(\left\{\begin{array}{l}4x + 4y = 7\\y = \frac{3}{4}x\end{array}\right.\)</para>
      </problem>
  </exercise>
  <!--Do not edit below this line-->
  <solution> 
  <para>Correct! Replacing x with 1 and y with \frac{3}{4} in both equations makes both equations true.</para>
  </solution>
  <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response"> 
  <para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.1.2.</para>
  </div>
</div>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="5" type="enumerated">
  <item>Solve the system of equations by graphing: \(\left\{\begin{array}{l}3x + y = -3\\2x + 3y = 5\end{array}\right.\)</item>
</list>
<div class="os-raise-ib-desmos-gc" data-schema-version="1.0"/>
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="56dba2fe-8bdc-40cd-b2f1-bf4e5e3b7b51" data-retry-limit="2" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <exercise data-content-id="26e7af8f-b850-444d-9fb7-bd02e90ede73" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="(-2,3)" data-solution-options="[&quot;(-2,3)&quot;, &quot;(0,-3)&quot;, &quot;(-3,6)&quot;, &quot;(4,-1)&quot;]">
    <problem>
    </problem>
  </exercise>
  <solution> 

  </solution>
  <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response"> 
    <para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.1.2.</para>
    </div>
  </div>
<!-- Question 6 -->
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="6" type="enumerated">
  <item>Solve the system of equations by graphing: \(\left\{\begin{array}{l}y = x + 2\\y = -2x + 2\end{array}\right.\)</item>
</list>
<div class="os-raise-ib-desmos-gc" data-schema-version="1.0"/>
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="4341dce1-55df-4952-aca1-e9feb69438d8" data-retry-limit="2" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <exercise data-content-id="39eb3a30-dad1-4781-b9f1-d0425a886b16" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="(0,2)" data-solution-options="[&quot;(2,0)&quot;, &quot;(-1,4)&quot;, &quot;(0,2)&quot;, &quot;(-2,0)&quot;]">
    <problem>
    </problem>
  </exercise>
  <solution> 
  <para>Correct! After graphing the two lines, they intersect at the point (0,2) so that is the solution for the system of equations.</para>
  </solution>
  <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response"> 
  <para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.1.2.</para>
  </div>
</div>
<!-- Question 7 -->
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="7" type="enumerated">
  <item>Solve the system of equations by graphing: \(\left\{\begin{array}{l}y = \frac{3}{2}x + 1\\y = -\frac{1}{2}x + 5\end{array}\right.\)</item>
</list>
<div class="os-raise-ib-desmos-gc" data-schema-version="1.0"/>
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="ea7d3b87-3226-4588-bbe0-998cf0869045" data-retry-limit="2" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <exercise data-content-id="aa410934-3bff-419f-a3b7-87cc2575d70c" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="(2,4)" data-solution-options="[&quot;(4,3)&quot;, &quot;(0,1)&quot;, &quot;(0,5)&quot;, &quot;(2,4)&quot;]">
    <problem>
    </problem>
  </exercise>
  <solution> 
    <para>Correct! After graphing the two lines, they intersect at the point (2,4) so that is the solution for the system of equations..</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response"> 
    <para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.1.2.</para>
    </div>
</div>
<!-- Question 8 -->
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="8" type="enumerated">
  <item>Solve the system of equations by graphing: \(\left\{\begin{array}{l}x + y = -4\\-x + 2y = -2\end{array}\right.\)</item>
</list>
<div class="os-raise-ib-desmos-gc" data-schema-version="1.0"/>
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="897173ce-61e5-44b3-b784-d2c9943c3b3d" data-retry-limit="2" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <exercise data-content-id="51654b4a-b819-4b70-800b-2141bb4cf1d4" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="(-2,-2)" data-solution-options="[&quot;(2,0)&quot;, &quot;(-1,0)&quot;, &quot;(4,1)&quot;, &quot;(-2,-2)&quot;]">
    <problem>
    </problem>
  </exercise>
  <solution> 
    <para>Correct! After graphing the two lines, they intersect at the point (-2,-2) so that is the solution for the system of equations.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response"> 
    <para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.1.2.</para>
    </div>
</div>
<!-- Question 9 -->
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="9" type="enumerated">
  <item>Solve the system of equations by graphing: \(\left\{\begin{array}{l}-2x + 3y = 3\\x + 3y = 12\end{array}\right.\)</item>
</list>
<div class="os-raise-ib-desmos-gc" data-schema-version="1.0"/>
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="d02ee8fa-7a39-4ac7-af2f-ddb85c4313a7" data-retry-limit="2" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <exercise data-content-id="7b9c0347-06f5-42e1-9185-c7c8dfa32680" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="(3,3)" data-solution-options="[&quot;(6,2)&quot;, &quot;(4,0)&quot;, &quot;(3,3)&quot;, &quot;(0,1)&quot;]">
    <problem>
    </problem>
  </exercise>
  <solution> 
    <para>Correct! After graphing the two lines, they intersect at the point (3,3) so that is the solution for the system of equations.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response"> 
    <para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.1.2.</para>
    </div>
</div>
<!-- Question 10 -->
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="10" type="enumerated">
  <item>Solve the system of equations by graphing: \(\left\{\begin{array}{l}2x - 4y = 8\\x + 3y = 9\end{array}\right.\)</item>
</list>
<div class="os-raise-ib-desmos-gc" data-schema-version="1.0"/>
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="56145455-63bc-457d-9673-7491bede8dfa" data-retry-limit="2" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <exercise data-content-id="df3a9916-9609-40e8-96e8-de3741236d91" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="(6,1)" data-solution-options="[&quot;(6,1)&quot;, &quot;(4,0)&quot;, &quot;(-2,0)&quot;, &quot;(8,2)&quot;]">
    <problem>
    </problem>
  </exercise>
  <solution> 
    <para>Correct! After graphing the two lines, they intersect at the point (6,1) so that is the solution for the system of equations.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response"> 
    <para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.1.2.</para>
    </div>
</div>
<!-- Question 11 -->
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="11" type="enumerated">
  <item>A bakery charges $2 per croissant and $4 per muffin. One day, they charge $42 in total and sell 15 baked goods. How many croissants and muffins did they sell?</item>
</list>

<div class="os-raise-ib-desmos-gc" data-schema-version="1.0" data-left="-2" data-right="20" data-top="20" data-bottom="-2"/>

<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="9d4b41c5-835e-41e2-ad40-c2e81e983c4d" data-retry-limit="2" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <exercise data-content-id="9e9ade08-25a7-44cc-8681-d0c47f2f2da0" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="9 croissants and 6 muffins" data-solution-options="[&quot;5 croissants and 10 muffins&quot;, &quot;9 croissants and 6 muffins&quot;, &quot;10 croissants and 5 muffins&quot;, &quot;8 croissants and 7 muffins&quot;]">
    <problem>
    </problem>
  </exercise>
  <solution> 
    <para>Correct! The answer is 9 croissants and 6 muffins. This is where the graphs intersect.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response"> 
    <para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.1.2.</para>
    </div>
</div>
<!-- Question 12 -->
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="12" type="enumerated">
  <item>A pet store sells mice for $7 each and gerbils for $9 each. They sell 17 animals for a total of $137. How many mice and gerbils did they sell?</item>
</list>
<div class="os-raise-ib-desmos-gc" data-schema-version="1.0" data-left="-2" data-right="20" data-top="20" data-bottom="-2"/>
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="0efe89e1-92da-4549-8eda-8df6f77729ae" data-retry-limit="2" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <exercise data-content-id="59fc72e4-1b49-40e3-aedd-6a834435cefa" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="8 mice and 9 gerbils" data-solution-options="[&quot;15 mice and 2 gerbils&quot;, &quot;8 mice and 9 gerbils&quot;, &quot;7 mice and 10 gerbils&quot;, &quot;6 mice and 11 gerbils&quot;]">
    <problem>
    </problem>
  </exercise>
  <solution> 
    <para>Correct! The answer is 8 mice and 9 gerbils. This is where the graphs intersect.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response"> 
    <para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.1.2.</para>
    </div>
</div></section>
</content>
